 thin, and this year's shift is a noticeable tilt. Relative humidity has fallen by about 1 point per decade, roughly 7 points since 1951; because warmer air holds more moisture, this does not necessarily mean the air is drier. El Niño may have an effect toward a more humid Mar–May, though the evidence is thin, and this year's shift is a noticeable tilt. For Mar–May 2027, a warmer-than-normal season is likely (about 70% chance), about 0.9 °C above the 1991–2020 average, mostly because of the long-term warming trend rather than El Niño. The El Niño expected for Sep–Nov 2026 is stronger than any in the record used here, so the outlook extends the historical relationship beyond what has been observed. This outlook is based on the El Niño strength expected for Sep–Nov 2026 and will be updated when it is observed in early December.","variables":{"temperature":{"normal_1991_2020":17.7628,"trend_per_decade":0.3647,"trend_p":0.0,"trend_total_since_1951":2.7351,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.0136,"enso_p":0.8778,"confidence":"No identifiable effect","survives_fdr":false,"fraction_explained":0.0003,"intrinsic_sd":0.7001,"effect_this_season":0.0256,"effect_ratio":0.0365,"size":"Negligible","size_typical_el_nino":"Negligible","once_every_n_years_without_el_nino":null,"expected_anomaly_2027":0.8666,"forecast_mean":18.6294,"forecast_sd":0.7486,"p_below":0.0785,"p_near":0.2225,"p_above":0.6991,"forecast_words":"Likely (70%): a warmer-than-normal season","within_record":false,"enso_effect_shrunk_per_degC":0.0101,"shrink_factor":0.7442,"effect_this_season_raw":0.0344,"trend_part_2027":0.841,"roni_upper_within_record":false,"years_of_warming_equivalent":0.7011,"percentiles":{"p05":{"trend_per_decade":0.3655,"trend_p":0.0002,"enso_effect_per_degC":-0.4125,"enso_p":0.027,"confidence":"Clear","shift_this_season":-1.0436,"lines_cross":false},"p50":{"trend_per_decade":0.4572,"trend_p":0.0,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.1958,"enso_p":0.1177,"confidence":"No identifiable effect","shift_this_season":0.49